{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-f2-reviewer-fable-30","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:d288f3b6bbda69d32acf","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"The report's selected result (pooled two-sample t-test of anet_umol_m2_s by salinity_regime, t(94) = 5.99, p < 0.0001, rejecting equality at the 5% level) is not supported at the declared independent unit. The data description names seedling_id as the independent unit (12 seedlings, 8 leaf readings each; treatment applied to whole pots), yet the workflow feeds all 96 leaf rows into scipy.stats.ttest_ind as independent observations. Aggregating to one mean per seedling (ambient: 11.50, 12.10, 12.50, 12.80, 13.40, 13.90; elevated: 10.60, 10.90, 11.40, 12.10, 12.40, 12.80) preserves the 1.000 umol CO2 m^-2 s^-1 mean difference but yields pooled t(10) = 1.99, below the two-sided 5% critical value 2.228 (p = 0.075). The claimed significance is an artifact of counting 8 correlated within-seedling readings as independent, inflating degrees of freedom from 10 to 94.","root_cause":"values_by_regime() appends one value per CSV row into per-regime lists and passes them directly to stats.ttest_ind(equal_var=True), which assumes each element is independent. Although the script defines UNIT_COLUMN = \"seedling_id\" and counts seedlings in seedlings_by_regime(), that grouping is used only for narrative text, never in inference. Each seedling therefore contributes 8 repeated entries to a row-independent procedure, producing 48 pseudo-observations per regime, 94 df instead of 10, and a p-value (< 0.0001) that overstates the evidence; the correct seedling-level test does not reject at the 5% level (p = 0.075).","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description declares seedling_id as the independent unit and one row as a single leaf reading, i.e., rows are subsamples within seedlings.","observed_value":"Independent unit column: seedling_id; one row = one leaf reading","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":24,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"One row is: one gas-exchange reading taken from one leaf of one mangrove seedling\nIndependent unit column: seedling_id"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":27,"end_line":28,"quoted_text":"The salinity treatment was applied to whole pots rather than to individual\nleaves, so the treatment label varies between seedlings and never within one."}]},{"description":"The workflow buckets one value per CSV row into per-regime lists and runs a pooled two-sample t-test directly on those row-level lists, with no aggregation by seedling.","observed_value":"96 leaf rows passed to ttest_ind; df computed as 48+48-2 = 94","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":35,"end_line":39,"quoted_text":"def values_by_regime(rows):\n    buckets = OrderedDict((name, []) for name in REGIMES)\n    for row in rows:\n        buckets[row[REGIME_COLUMN]].append(float(row[VALUE_COLUMN]))\n    return buckets"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":69,"end_line":72,"quoted_text":"outcome = stats.ttest_ind(buckets[ambient], buckets[elevated], equal_var=True)\n    tstat = float(outcome.statistic)\n    pvalue = float(outcome.pvalue)\n    df = len(buckets[ambient]) + len(buckets[elevated]) - 2"}]},{"description":"The report explicitly asserts that each row is one observation, claims 48 observations per regime and 94 degrees of freedom, and bases its rejection at the 5% level on that test.","observed_value":"t(94) = 5.99, p < 0.0001","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"Two-sided two-sample Student t-test with pooled variance\n(scipy.stats.ttest_ind, equal_var=True). Each row of data/input.csv supplies\none observation, giving 48 observations per regime and 94 degrees of freedom."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Two-sample pooled t-test of anet_umol_m2_s by salinity_regime: t(94) = 5.99, p < 0.0001; ambient_15ppt mean 12.700 vs elevated_35ppt mean 11.700, difference 1.000 umol CO2 m^-2 s^-1."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":29,"end_line":31,"quoted_text":"Assimilation averages 1.000 umol CO2 m^-2 s^-1 higher under ambient than under\nelevated salinity; the pooled t-test rejects equality of the two regime means\nat the conventional 5 percent level."}]},{"description":"The CSV confirms the repeated-unit structure: e.g., seedling MG01 contributes eight rows (M001-M008), all under one treatment label, and every other seedling likewise contributes eight rows.","observed_value":"8 rows per seedling_id; 12 seedlings; 96 rows","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"M001,MG01,ambient_15ppt,1,11.60\nM002,MG01,ambient_15ppt,2,11.35\nM003,MG01,ambient_15ppt,3,11.70\nM004,MG01,ambient_15ppt,4,11.45\nM005,MG01,ambient_15ppt,5,11.30\nM006,MG01,ambient_15ppt,6,11.65\nM007,MG01,ambient_15ppt,7,11.40\nM008,MG01,ambient_15ppt,8,11.55"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow is aware of the unit column: it defines UNIT_COLUMN = 'seedling_id' and correctly reports the design (12 seedlings, 8 readings per seedling, 6 per regime) in the report narrative. However, this awareness is used only for descriptive text, not for the statistical test, so it does not negate the issue.","observed_value":"UNIT_COLUMN defined and design correctly described, but unused in inference","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":17,"end_line":19,"quoted_text":"REGIME_COLUMN = \"salinity_regime\"\nUNIT_COLUMN = \"seedling_id\"\nVALUE_COLUMN = \"anet_umol_m2_s\""},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":7,"end_line":8,"quoted_text":"Design: 12 Avicennia marina seedlings, 8 gas-exchange readings per seedling;\n6 seedlings at 15 ppt (ambient_15ppt) and 6 at 35 ppt (elevated_35ppt)."}]},{"description":"The direction and magnitude of the descriptive effect are robust: seedling-level aggregation gives the same group means (12.700 vs 11.700) and mean difference (1.000) as the row-level summary, so the point estimate in the report is not itself distorted; only the inferential claim is.","observed_value":"seedling-level means 12.700 vs 11.700, difference 1.000 (matches report)","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":12,"end_line":15,"quoted_text":"| salinity_regime | rows | mean | SD |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| ambient_15ppt | 48 | 12.700 | 0.816 |\n| elevated_35ppt | 48 | 11.700 | 0.818 |"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to show the conclusion survives a unit-correct reanalysis. Computing per-seedling means from data/input.csv by hand: ambient (MG01-MG06) = 11.50, 12.10, 12.50, 12.80, 13.40, 13.90 (mean 12.70, sum of squared deviations 3.78); elevated (MG07-MG12) = 10.60, 10.90, 11.40, 12.10, 12.40, 12.80 (mean 11.70, sum of squared deviations 3.80). Pooled variance = (3.78+3.80)/10 = 0.758; SE of the difference = sqrt(0.758 x (1/6+1/6)) = 0.5027; t = 1.000/0.5027 = 1.99 on 10 df, below the two-sided 5% critical value of 2.228 (p = 0.075), so equality is not rejected. I also verified the report's own leaf-level numbers are internally consistent (means 12.700/11.700, SDs 0.816/0.818 imply t = 6.0 on 94 df, matching t(94) = 5.99), confirming the discrepancy stems solely from treating 96 correlated rows as independent, not from a computational error. The falsification failed: the reported significance does not survive analysis at the declared independent unit.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}